From: openhc-minecraft
Subject: [PATCH] FPE: per-vertex fog by GL_FOG_HINT, unprojected 2D sampling when q is 1

GL_FOG_HINT was ignored on ES2 backends; fog was always computed per pixel,
from a highp varying and a length() in every fragment. Fixed-function GL lets
fog be per vertex, and the code for it was there but compiled out: it is now
chosen per state, for GL_FOG_HINT GL_FASTEST, or for GL_DONT_CARE when
LIBGL_VERTEXFOG=1. On a PowerVR SGX545 that is ~10% more frame rate in
Minecraft, which has fog on everything.

Also: when a 2D texture unit's coordinate q is known to be 1 (no texgen on Q,
an affine texture matrix, at most 3 components, or a display list whose q are
all 1), texture2D on .st can replace texture2DProj, which some GPUs prefetch.
Off by default (LIBGL_TEX2DNOPROJ=1 turns it on): on SGX545 with DDK 1.7 the
plain lookups lock the GPU up repeatedly.

